<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ulster Bank sees further Irish growth.</title>
<headline>Ulster Bank sees further Irish growth.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ulster Bank, the wholly owned subsidiary of NatWest Plc, said on Tuesday that further growth was planned for the group.</p>
<p>&quot;New branches and new services will be introduced and, with general economic conditions remaining favourable the overall prospects for business continue to be positive,&quot; Ronnie Kells, Group Chief Executive, Ulster Bank, said.</p>
</text>
